\title{Terminal object}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2026-10-31T03:13:08Z}
\author{hsuchingchung}
\import{macros-subobj}

\p{Let \CCat be a category. An object #{1} in \CCat is called a \strong{terminal object} of \CCat if for any object #{A} in \CCat, there exists a unique morphism from #{A} to #{1}. Explicitly,

\ul{

\li{we have a morphism #{\bang_A : A \r 1} for each object #{A} in \CCat, and}

\li{for any morphism #{f : A \r 1}, we have #{f = \bang_A}.}
}

}